ion by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  91  to chromosome 17 signals  89  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The repeat hormone receptor stains  as requested by the clinician  confirm previous results  Uninvolved breast epithelium adjacent to the carcinoma focally shows estrogen  and progesterone receptor positive cells  this serves as an internal positive control of the hormone receptor staining and supports the result  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  3 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  FURTHER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINS TO EVALUATE SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  Immunohistochemical studies performed on paraffin sections of the left axillary sentinel node reveal large paracortical nodules of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive dendritic cells  There is an appropriate architectural distribution of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive lymphocytes  These findings support a reactive process with dermatopathic features  There is no evidence of lymphoma  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  4 by Robert Hasserjian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   NON SENTINEL    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MARGIN  SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY    EXCI PART E  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MARGIN  INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY    EXCI , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 16 19 CLINICAL DATA  Fifty four year old white female with biopsy proven right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  FOCAL RESIDUAL INTRADUCTAL AND INVASIVE DUCT CARCINOMA  NIPPLE AND DEEP MARGIN OF RESECTION ARE NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  A SINGLE FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  TWENTY TWO OF 22 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  SEE NOTE  NOTE  One axillary lymph node contains non caseating granulomas  Special stains for acid fast bacilli and fungi are negative  2  FAT NECROSIS  FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION AND GRANULATION TISSUE FORMATION CONSISTENT WITH PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE  3  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Carol A  Filomena  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 12 16                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh labeled  right breast  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of 25 x 19 x 7 0cm right breast  a 25 x 9 0cm skin ellipse  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm attached axillary tissue  The nipple is 1 0cm in diameter  the areola is 4 0cm in diameter  both are unremarkable  10 0cm from the nipple is a 2 5cm long biopsy incision  partially healed  covered by Tegaderm  Beneath the incision is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm stellate  hard  white  focally brown mass  extending to within 0 5cm of the deep margin  and is surrounded by indurated hemorrhagic breast  Section Code A D   representative sections of mass and adjacent deep margin  medial to lateral E   anterior lateral section of mass F   slightly firm area with cyst  6cm medial to mass G   representative section of nipple H M   nodes from axillary tail  largest 2 0cm in diameter  all firm and pink  I  K  individual nodes sectioned  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 41 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old lady who had one focus of DCIS on a needle localization biopsy peformed August 12th of this year  She had a re excision biopsy of the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  NOTE  No blood or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 22 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 52     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with an associated skin ellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and contains a healed scar that runs in a vertical direction  A safety pin was placed to denote the superior aspect of the specimen  The specimen was inked and sectioned to reveal  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity filled with red clot  The closest margin to the biopsy cavity is the anterior surface which is 0 2cm away  In addition  there are two cystic spaces  One measuring 0 2cm in diameter and the other 0 1cm in diameter in the most superior aspect of the specimens  Section Code  A  biopsy cavity with anterior margin  anterior margin has the largest straight surface area   B  biopsy cavity with anterior  long  and medial  short  margins C  biopsy cavity with anterior  short  and posterior  long  resection margin D  representative section of inferior portion of specimen  the anterior margin is not inked  E  superior resection margin  en face including two cystic areas F  biopsy cavity with anterior margin  G  biopsy cavity with the posterior margins inked H  biopsy cavity has been removed  this is the posterior  long  inferior  short  resection margins I  biopsy cavity has been excised  posterior  long  inferior  short  resection margin are included  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Barbara Joyce Nath  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
