Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 AUG 94 at 11 29 CLINICAL DATA  72 year old female with a history of right breast cancer with mastectomy   REMOVED_CASE_ID    she now has dimpling of the left nipple  Biopsy  left breast diagnosed intraductal carcinoma  REMOVED_CASE_ID  treated with radiation only                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY OF LARGE MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  INVOLVING THE ENTIRE BIOPSY SPECIMEN INCLUDING THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 94 at 14 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty f