ist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a tan pink soft tissue which mostly represents a lymph node with a small amount of fat surrounding it  The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1 and  1A  now resubmitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  The surrounding remaining fat is entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast simple mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5 cm right simple mastectomy with a short stitch indicating 12 o clock  The anterior aspect of the main specimen is inked blue  and the posterior aspect is inked black  The overlying 30 x 19 2 cm tan skin ellipse contains a 6 x 4 cm areola with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0 cm unremarkable nipple  No scars are identified  Underlying the nipple areolar complex is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7 cm biopsy cavity  lined by smooth tan tissue with surrounding yellow punctate areas and focal grittiness  The cavity is 2cm from the posterior resection margin  4 2cm from the skin ellipse and 7 3cm from the anterior resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is multifocally fibrotic  No lymph nodes are detected in the axillary portion of the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity  entirely submitted  with surrounding gritty areas from medial to lateral  with closest deep resection margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity  medially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity  laterally  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 1A  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  NO TUMOR SEEN  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electro