o the nipple is a 2 5cm well healed linear scar with an adjacent REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm blue stained area  The remaining skin surface is unremarkable  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm previous biopsy cavity located within the mid to lateral aspect of the specimen  coming to 0 7cm from the overlying free moving posterior margin and 2 1cm from the overlying scar bearing skin  The cavity is empty and has a gray white  smooth and glistening lining  The cavity borders are rubbery and fibrotic with areas of focal hemorrhage and fat necrosis  The surrounding and remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink  lobulated  fibrofatty tissue with no discrete masses or lesions identified  No lymph nodes are palpated along the periphery  Representative sections are submitted as follows  D F  Entire cavity to deep margin  G M  Uninvolved fibrous tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen with a suture designating the 12 o clock aspect  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 10 2cm tan white skin ellipse with a centrally located REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  No scar is identified along the skin surface  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan pink  indurated and well delineated stellate mass located within the mid portion of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and coming to 1 6cm from the overlying free moving posterior margin and 3 9cm from the unremarkable overlying skin surface  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan pink to yellow  lobulated and unremarkable with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified  No lymph nodes are palpated along the periphery  Representative sections are submitted as follows  N 