itive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 94 at 14 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number in two parts  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of pink tan  rubbery tissue  bisected and submitted entirely in cassette A  Received is a 630 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 9 2cm skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The skin ellipse contains a 0 9cm nipple  4 8cm areola  0 8cm from the inferior skin margin and 7 5cm from the medial margin and a 4 6cm linear  well healed scar  2 0cm from the areola in the upper outer quadrant  There is a palpable REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm slightly mobile mass which is fixed to the skin  the skin overlying the mass appears normal  The subcutaneous tissue is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm lobulated to stellate  white gray mass with focal light yellow  soft focus  0 2cm from the skin surface and extending to within 0 4cm of the inked deep margin and 1 5cm from the inked superior margin  There are multiple discrete  white grey firm nodules adjacent to this mass  up to 1 0cm in diameter  The remaining tissue consists of yellow  soft  fibroadipose tissue and white pink breast parenchyma  Eleven