Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 15 09 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  80   INVADING LYMPHATICS  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  AND DISPLAYING SOME FEATURES SUGGESTIVE OF NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  20   CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 16 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  Left breast mass   is a 3 x 2 x 1 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned  revealing a firm  gray area  REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 5cm  abutting the margin at one pole  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and submitted in A  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in B through D  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  CARCINOMA  SUSPICIOUS FOR NEUROENDOCRINE CARCINOMA  INVADING LOBULES  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Stephen Bowman Trippel  M D  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
