he breast is 20 x 12 x 4cm  The skin ellipse is REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm with a 1 0cm diameter unremarkable nipple and a 3 5cm diameter unremarkable areola  2 0cm superior and lateral to the nipple is a 6 0cm recently sutured incision  Deep to this is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm defect in the specimen which corresponds to the previously lumpectomy specimen  The defect is complete in this area without a deep margin  the deep margin of the previous lumpectomy is described by the surgeon as to the fascia   The skin ellipse also contains three slightly raised brown to purple macules  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The remainder of the breast specimen contains soft  white yellow unremarkable breast parenchyma  The axillary tail is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  from which multiple soft  tan to pink lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension are dissected  SECTION CODE  M T  axillary tail lymph nodes  O and S  one lymph node each bisected  U V  representative deep resection margins  inferior to previous biopsy site W  representative section  inferior to lumpectomy defect X  representative sections of skin  anterior to lumpectomy defect Y  representative sections of nipple X  representative section of breast  at least 2 0cm from the lumpectomy incision  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST SUBAREOLAR RESECTION MARGIN   POSITIVE FOR INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  William H  Yong  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST SUBAREOLAR DUCT PART B  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY PART C  COMPLETION LEFT TISSUE MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
