Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 57 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVOLVING INKED SURGICAL MARGINS  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  FOCAL  NOTE  The tumor measures 0 9cm in greatest dimension  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 36                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   0   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 14     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast tissue  The specimen is inked  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 8cm  stellate  tan mass adjacent to an inked margin  surrounded by rubbery  white tissue  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1 and saved  The specimen is entirely submitted in A through E  Stellate mass submitted in A and B  Resident  David Andrews  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   RADICAL SCAR VERSUS WELL DIFFERENTIATED ADENOCARCINOMA EXTENDING TO INKED MARGIN  AWAIT PERMANENTS FOR FINAL DIAGNOSIS  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
