adical mastectomy specimen consists of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm  an overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 12 5cm  axillary fat tissue REMOVED_DATE x 7 6cm  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of skeletal muscle  There is no cutaneous incision visible  nor is there a nipple or areola present  On the cutaneous surface there is an ulcer measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm  It is yellow  and hemorrhagic with red yellow rolled edges  It is 9 2cm from the lateral skin margin  6 2cm from the medial skin margin  3 2cm from the superior skin margin  and 4 5cm from the inferior skin margin  Lateral and inferior to the ulcer there is a small yellow firm lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The skin surrounding the ulcer is violaceous and mottled  Within the parenchyma there is a firm  white  ill defined mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm  The axillary portion is dissected for lymph nodes  however none are found  Section Code  A  frozen section  1  medial   B  frozen section  2  lateral   C  frozen section  3  superior   D  frozen section  4  inferior   E G  inferior portion of axilla from the left breast  H J  middle third axilla from the left breast  K N  superior portion of axilla from the left breast  O Q  inferior region of axilla of the right breast  R S  largest node in the middle axilla of the right breast  T  external portion of the large node in the right breast  U W  superior axilla from the right breast  X  right nipple  en face  Y  skin papule from the right breast  Z  right nipple  radial section  AA  closest deep margin of the right breast  BB  closest inferior margin of the right breast  CC FF  four representative sections of the mass biopsy cavity  GG  cyst  representative section of the right breast  HH  parenchyma of the right breast behind the nipple  II JJ  parenchyma of the right breast  KK  skin of biopsy cavity  right breast  LL  closest deep margin of the left breast  MM PP  representative sections of t