Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 42 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma  Left breast biopsy on REMOVED_DATE revealed both ductal carcinoma in situ and infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  60    SOLID AND COMEDO TYPE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The inked resection margins are negative for carcinoma  The residual tumor measures approximately 2cm in greatest dimension  There is no evidence of malignancy in 11 out of 11 lymph nodes  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES INCLUDING FIBROSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA MICROCYST FORMATION  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATION  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 08                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a right breast  REMOVED_DATE x 17 x 4cm  an overlying skin ellipse  REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm  axillary tail  11 x 6 x 2 5cm and thin strips of skeletal muscle  4 x 2 x 0 5cm  The entire specimen weighs 580 grams  3cm inferior to the nipple is a 12 5cm long curved  healed incision  Beneath this is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm cystic cavity filled with blood clot  This cavity has a smooth  firm wall and is 1cm away from the deep resection margin  The parenchyma around the cavity is indurated and hemorrhagic  Adjacent to the cavity  superiorly an 11 x 7 x 2 5cm  tan  firm  focally gritty and cystic  stellate rubbery parenchyma is present  This rubbery parenchyma extends to 0 4cm from the deepest margin  to 2cm from the medial resection margin  and 3cm from the axillary tail  The remaining parenchyma is soft  yellow  lobulated  The nipple is retracted  The axillary nodes are as large as 1 2cm in diameter and soft  tan  Section Code A B   mass C   deepest resection margin adjacent to the cavity  D G   other closest margins from the remaining firm areas  H   representative medial rubbery area  I   representative central rubbery area near cavity  J   representative central rubbery area away from the cavity  K   representative lateral rubbery area near the axillary portion  L   nipple  M   skin through the incision  N Q   nodes from axillary tail Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
