Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 43 CLINICAL DATA  Core diagnosis IDC                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  LUMPECTOMY   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO THE POSTERIOR MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM   LOW GRADE  PRESENT AT THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL NODE  1   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  2   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  3   EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL BREAST MARGINS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PRESENT IN 3 OF 4 TISSUE BLOCKS  THE LARGEST FOCUS IN A SINGLE SLIDE SPANS REMOVED_DATE CM   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN DESIGNATED BY THE SUTURE  AND PRESENT AT THE MARGIN OPPOSITE THAT DESIGNATED BY THE SUTURE  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Residual invasive carcinoma is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 41                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF KERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 58     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a tan  yellow  irregular 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of breast tissue infiltrated with blue dye  The specimen is inked black  The posterior is overinked blue  the superior is overinked with yellow and sectioned to reveal a stellate 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass that focally abuts the posterior margin  SECTION CODE A D  Tumor  with  almost entirely submitted  closest margins in A and B  E F  Representative sections of breast not involving tumor  Also received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm piece of yellow tan tissue which is bisected and totally submitted in G  Also received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  2  is a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of yellow tan firm lymph node which is bisected and totally submitted in H  Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  3  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of yellow tan lymph node which is bisected and totally submitted in I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left additional breast margins  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of oriented fibroadipose tissue  There is an undesignated suture on one aspect  The entire specimen is inked black  The sutured margin is overinked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly unremarkable fibrous tissue with minute cystic changes  No discrete lesions are noted  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes J through M  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA ABUTTING THE POSTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  TAN A  INCE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT   LUMPECTOMY PART B  LYMPN NODE LEFT AXILLARY  1  EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  2  EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLARY  3  EXCISION PART E  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGINS    EXCISIONAL BIO   report_end  , Unchecked.
