meter and bears an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unremarkable  everted nipple  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm previous biopsy cavity containing organized clotted blood  0 1cm from the posterior margin and abutting the anterior margin  The specimen was received unoriented  therefore  the orientation is designated based on the location of the biopsy site  which is presumed to be within the central to upper outer aspect of the breast  There are 2 adjacent firm masses abutting the previous biopsy cavity  located at the superior and inferior aspects of the cavity  up to REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE in greatest dimensions  These areas are focally abutting the anterior and posterior margins  Further sectioning reveals an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm portion of dense gray white  gritty fibrous tissue immediately adjacent to the biopsy cavity and extending medially to the upper and lower inner quadrants  There are 5 firm masses identified within this gritty fibrous tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  within 0 3cm of the posterior margin and 0 5cm of the anterior margin  These areas are ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 6 5cm from the previous biopsy cavity  There is an additional firm mass located in the upper outer quadrant  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  0 2cm from the anterior margin and abutting the posterior margin  This area is located 0 3cm from the previous biopsy cavity  which may be continuous with this mass  The upper outer aspect of the specimen is dissected and palpated  however  no lymph nodes are grossly identified  Also in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is sectioned to reveal yellow  lobulated  homogenous cut surfaces  with no masses  lesions or candidate lymph nodes identified  Also in