  carcinoma cells appear pleomorphic and of ductal type  a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  immunostain shows those carcinoma cells to be located in a lymphatic vessel   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TEN LYMPH NODES  0 10    SEE TABLE  2    SEE NOTE 2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  1 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  20 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   1 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   0 Extracapsular extension  None Other forms of axillary involvement  None NOTE  2  Several lymph nodes show focal fibrosis and scarring  consistent with treatment effect after neoadjuvant chemotherapy  Definitive carcinoma is not identified on hematoxylin eosin sections  However  immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam REMOVED_DATE show that one lymph node in the area of the axillary tail contains a few cytokeratin positive large cells  which are favored to represent isolated tumor cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Cytokeratin stains on several other lymph nodes are negative  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm left breast modified radical mastectomy specimen  with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of axillary tissue and a short suture indicating superior and a long suture indicating lateral aspects  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 11 7cm ellipse of skin appears unremarkable  The REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm tan nipple and areolar complex appears unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan yellow fatty cut surface  with an abundant amount of interspersed dense  nodular gray white fibrous tissue  with focal cystic areas  These cystic areas range from REMOVED_DATE  0 3cm in diameter with surrounding yellowish discoloration  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The axillary fat on dissection reveals multiple lymph nodes  ranging from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the upper portion of the left breast  submitted from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   No tissue submitted  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  intact  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm area  upper outer quadrant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections from the upper portion of the left breast  Received in formalin  labeled  additional left axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm aggregate of multiple portions of tan yellow  lymph node bearing fat  which contains multiple possible lymph nodes  ranging from 0 5cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes  bisected  1 inked black   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 52 53PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  There are only few invasive carcinoma cells  less than 20   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 21   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 43 39PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  The section shows a small number of invasive tumor cells  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  34  to chromosome 17 signals  30  in 18 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 32 07PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  3  ADDITIONAL IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY RESULTS NOTE  The tumor cells analyzed for receptor strains and Her 2 protein expression in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  show a different profile than the original tumor  which had been characterized as estrogen  and progesterone receptor protein negative  and Her 2 overexpressing on the prior core biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   reviewed   Morphologically  the tumor cells identified in a lymphatic vessel of the mastectomy specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   resemble the patient s breast carcinoma before initiation of chemotherapy  However  this focus has nearly disappeared on a deeper section  which is why this block was not used for a repeat of receptor and Her 2 stains  It is concluded from those findings that the invasive carcinoma cells identified in the area of the tumor bed most likely represent another primary  which had not been previously sampled and is an incidental finding  Immunostains for estrogen  and progesterone receptor proteins  and for Her 2 protein were also performed on the lymph node showing isolated tumor cells  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    However  those are non contributory as no tumor cells are represented on the sections provided for immunohistochemical stains  No additional information on the hormone receptor or Her 2 profile of those isolated tumor cells can be provided  Dr Smith was notified about the additional findings by email on REMOVED_DATE  Addendum  3 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 02   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 41 42PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Modified Radical Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left Additional Axillary Tissue   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
