e deep  as well as another inked resection margin  The cystic cavity lies 1 7cm deep the skin ellipse  and lies focally at the deep  as well as one other inked resection margin  Apart from the biopsy cavity  a 1 0cm in diameter  white  shiny  firm area with irregular and ill defined borders approaches the deep inked resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is yellow  soft  and lobulated  SECTION CODE  A  skin with scar and biopsy cavity B D  biopsy cavity with closest inked resection  deep and side  E F  biopsy cavity  representative sections G H  firm area  entirely I  breast  representative section  Labeled  axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is dissected to reveal multiple  19  lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 9cm in greatest dimension  with tan to fatty cut surfaces  Submitted in J through O  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY NODES  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 97 at 10 27 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN  SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   CALCIFICATIONS IN MICROCYSTS  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  20 AUG 97 at 11 17 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrofatty parenchyma  as well as a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm area of papillarity  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through J  with suspicious areas for calcification in cassettes A   C  and the area of papillarity in cassette A  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST MASS   NO LESIONS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Barbara Joyce Nath  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY , Unchecked.
