Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 35 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS close to edge single sutures  long   lateral  short   superior  double suture   most posterior margin side away from tumor bed                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 26 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The posterior surface is marked by a double stitch  lateral surface is marked by a long stitch  the superior surface is marked by a short stitch  The posterior surface consists of fibroadipose tissue and is grossly unremarkable  The anterior surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE white fibrinous area that extends to the lateral margin  a rubbery REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow well circumscribed nodule that extends to the medial border  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan yellow nodule that extends to within 0 3cm of the lateral superior border  On the anterior surface there are also several focal greenish gray regions ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm the remainder of the anterior surface has focal areas of hemorrhage  The posterior surface is inked in black  the anterior surface is inked in blue  and the superior posterior surface is overinked in yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal  The medial nodule has a yellow cut surface with areas of apparent fatty necrosis  superior lateral nodule has a yellow white cut surface with focal areas of hemorrhage  the fibrinous biopsy cavity has a yellow white cut surface the remainder of the parenchyma has a yellow white cut surface and is grossly unremarkable  Section code  A  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity nearest to the margin at the inferior aspect of the specimen  B  Representative sections of the medial nodule  C  Representative sections of the superior lateral nodule  D  Representative section of the biopsy cavity near the superior margin  E  Representative section of the parenchyma at the superior margin  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Thor Stein  M D  Signed Out by  Adriana Dionigi Corben  M D  CLINICAL DATA  55 year old woman status post chemotherapy for locally advanced triple negative left breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  UPPER INNER QUADRANT HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  1   2  FLAT EPITHELIAL ATYPIA  3  PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  4  CALCIFICATIONS IN FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  IN SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND IN BENIGN LOBULES  5  FIFTEEN LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES WITH NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  2   NOTE  1  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm upper inner quadrant tumor bed  which includes a healing biopsy site  has been entirely submitted  It consists of vascular fibroelastotic stroma containing lymphocytes  giant cells  hemosiderin laden macrophages and histiocytes  Multiple immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 do not disclose invasive carcinoma  post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Miller Payne Grading System  grade 5   There is no evidence of in situ ductal carcinoma  The resection margins are free of tumor  Lymphovascular invasion is not identified  NOTE  2  8 of the 15 negative axillary lymph nodes show therapeutic effect  post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Sataloff Grading  N A   GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 23 x 17 x 3 8cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 5 x 4 5cm skin ellipse containing a central 1 4cm in diameter unremarkable nipple  The specimen is oriented with a long stitch designating the lateral aspect and a short stitch designating the superior aspect of the specimen  The anterior resection margin is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm irregular tan white indurated area  tumor bed   which includes a biopsy site and is located in the upper inner quadrant of the breast  1 4cm from the closest posterior and 0 8cm from the closest anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable and no lesions are identified  Within the axillary tail  15 lymph nodes are identified  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 5cm indurated area  tumor bed   entirely submitted  with surrounding parenchyma and closest resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower inner breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper outer breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower outer breast quadrant  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   14 lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 13   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 17 30PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left   Modified Radical Mastectomy  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 AUG 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 AUG 95 at 09 41 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II III  PRESENT THROUGHOUT ALL THREE SPECIMENS AND EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS IN ALL THREE SPECIMENS  WITH LYMPHATIC VASCULAR INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  PRESENT THROUGHOUT ALL THREE SPECIMENS  3  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Lobular carcinoma in situ may also be present  Immunoperoxidase stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  09 AUG 95 at 16 25 Staff Pathologist  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 95 at 15 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   are three fragments of breast tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  respectively  with rubbery  white bands and ill defined  firm areas  A firm area from the largest fragment is frozen and saved frozen  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes A through N  The largest fragment is in A G  the smaller fragments are in H J  and the remaining undesignated tissue is in K N  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO A MARGIN  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
